## Context

The data paper documents a new JETP dataset, distinct from the existing repository data-paper deliverable. Its contribution is consistent observation and transparent limits, not proof of acceleration.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First reproducibility acceptance check: an independent reader reconstructs one published country total and one timeline from a frozen release, dictionary and source locators. Any undocumented choice or unavailable required input is an explicit failure to fix.

## Actions

Create a distinct JETP data-paper outline and manuscript in the repository publication architecture. Describe collection, identities, sources, lifecycle states, missingness, conflicts, validation, release cadence and reuse. Quantify coverage rather than claiming universal completeness. Prepare a citable deposit package and verify its release identifier before finalising data-availability text. Choose a suitable venue with documented scope; do not submit as part of this ticket.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Reviewable manuscript, coverage tables and validation examples
- [ ] Dataset availability, version, reuse terms and citation are accurate
- [ ] Independent reproduction exercise recorded
- [ ] Claims distinguish source coverage from actual implementation performance
- [ ] Citable data package prepared and manuscript builds with resolved references

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.
